  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 319 AM EDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThursday and Friday, the same overall pattern continues. Upper \nridging over the Western States and an upper trough over the \nNortheast will continue pushing the large surface high towards the \nOhio Valley, keeping northeast winds across the CWA. This will limit \nhighs to the upper 70s to mid 80s with dew points in the 50s and low \n60s. \n\nBy Friday night, the center of the surface high will pass, just to \nour north. Return flow begins advecting precipitable water values \napproaching 2\" ahead of a shortwave flowing along the ridge. This is \nexpected to increase rain chances into the day on Saturday. The best \nchances of precipitation is expected across southern Kentucky, but \nshould be fairly uneventful with nothing severe. Temperatures start \nto climb, into the mid 80s on Saturday and the low 90s from Sunday \ninto the first part of next week.  \n\nInto next week, the overall pattern doesn't change. Additional \nchances for precipitation will be introduced as waves work towards \nthe Lower Ohio Valley on northwest flow, but nothing looks \nconcerning.",
